id: obscured
name: Obscured
kind: battlefield
envQuality: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  You cannot see out of it, and neither can anyone see into it. Strike Rolls, Dodge Rolls
  and Impulsive Saves 2(bT) lower.
text: >
  Obscured: While you occupy this Square, reduce your Strike Rolls, Dodge Rolls, and
  Impulsive Saves by 2(bT). This Environmental Quality can be applied to Squares within
  High Environments.

---

# "While you occupy this Square", which is the whole of the condition and is not written
# below: being gathered is what occupying it means.
#
# Three named rolls and not "all of your Combat Rolls", so this is three lines rather than
# `combatRolls` - the Wound Roll is a Combat Roll and is deliberately not among them. Smoke
# makes you harder to aim and harder to dodge with; it does not make your fist softer.
#
# The Impulsive Save is the Agility one, and the only Saving Throw named - so `save.impulsive`
# rather than `save.all`. A character choking in the smoke resists a mind-affecting effect
# exactly as well as they did.
#
# --- The last sentence ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "This Environmental Quality can be applied to Squares within High Environments." A
# permission about where the ARC may put it, and there are no High Environments yet. Carried
# in the text and built into nothing.

[passive]
strike -= 2(bT);
dodge -= 2(bT);
save.impulsive -= 2(bT);
